WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:03.460
- Every now and then I get
a friend or a family member

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.820
saying that they're interested in buying

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.730
some type of a business.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.230
So this wouldn't be about
starting a business,

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.620
but there might be an existing business.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.670
Maybe it's a convenience store

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.050
or maybe it's some type
of health care practice

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.410
or whatever it might be, and they say,

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.060
hey, I'm going to buy this
from the existing owner

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.400
and I think it's going
to be a great business.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.520
And they'll often say it
generates this much money

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.020
and I only have to put this much in

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.740
and it feels risk free.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.900
And what I tend to tell them,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.880
and I don't wanna be one
of these naysayer people,

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.780
I say, possibly.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.450
But what you always have to think about

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.620
is why are they selling it?

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.610
And sometimes there's a good
reason why they're selling it.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.430
Maybe they're retiring and they don't have

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.150
someone to pass the business onto

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:50.950
and they see in you kind of
the person that they would

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.170
love to see running that
business going forward.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.850
That could be a very legitimate thing.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.480
But oftentimes, there might be situations

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.370
where they might be pumping
up some of the numbers,

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.820
they might be showing you business

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.420
in the busy season or on the busy day.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.300
And so I wouldn't take, especially
if it's a small business

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.500
that doesn't have auditing,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.920
that doesn't have really
strict accounting practices.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.680
I would observe the business
for a very long period of time

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.730
and I would take your own data

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.950
as to whether the numbers
you're hearing about are real.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:24.120
And I also wouldn't
discount how much effort

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.640
and work the existing
owner is putting into it

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.470
and what happens to the business

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.430
if they're no longer there.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.190
If all of that works out

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.750
and if it really does make sense,

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.903
then, yeah, you might be onto something.

